<title>TURKEY: Turkish military jet crashes, two crew dead.</title>
<headline>Turkish military jet crashes, two crew dead.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>An F-4 warplane crashed after taking off from a military airport in central Turkey on Wednesday, killing the two crew, Anatolian news agency said.</p>
<p>It said the aircraft crashed in Konya province after hitting electricity power lines.</p>
<p>An investigation into the cause of the crash was continuing, the agency said.</p>
</text>
